ering'), Document(id='17a638e4-7c2f-4f98-94f3-930af3a1051f', metadata={'creationdate': '2021-10-26T07:05:00+00:00', 'creator': 'Microsoft® Word for Microsoft 365', 'moddate': '2021-10-26T07:05:00+00:00', 'page': 0, 'page_label': '1', 'producer': 'Microsoft® Word for Microsoft 365', 'source': '../rguktBasarDataset/other_files/PEO.pdf', 'total_pages': 4}, page_content='RAJIV GANDHI UNIVERSITY OF \nKNOWLEDGE TECHNOLOGIES, BASAR \n(Telangana Government Act 8 of 2016) \nBasar, Nirmal Dist, Telangana State. \n \n \nDEPARTMENT OF CIVIL ENGINEERING \n \n \nPROGRAMS OFFERED \n \n➢ Department offers only four years under graduation course in Civil Engineering currently. \n➢ Has highly qualified faculty from different disciplines of Civil Engineering. \n➢ Posses good Infrastructure and lab facilities. \n➢ Equipped with modern IT tools related to Civil Engineering'), Document(id='36f18027-5ce4-4aa2-957e-729dc1f862f9', metadata={'creationdate': "D:20241229171605Z00'00'", 'creator': 'Pages', 'moddate': "D:20241229171605Z00'00'", 'page': 0, 'page_label': '1', 'producer': 'macOS Version 15.1 (Build 24B83) Quartz PDFContext', 'source': '../rguktBasarDataset/about_rgukt/campusLife.pdf', 'title': 'campusLife', 'total_pages': 4}, page_content='Rajiv Gandhi University of Knowledge Technologies (RGUKT) Basar\nOverview:\n• Establishment: RGUKT Basar was established by the Government of Andhra Pradesh \n(A.P) in 2008 as a full-ﬂedged university.\n• Objective: The university was created to provide high-quality educational opportunities to \ntalented rural youth, primarily from Telangana and Andhra Pradesh.\n• Background:\n◦ The ﬁrst batch of 6,000 students was admitted to a six-year integrated program in \nAugust 2008.\n◦ Following the bifurcation of Andhra Pradesh in 2015, the campuses were divided \nbetween Telangana and Andhra Pradesh.\n◦ Currently, the Basar campus is the only one operational in Telangana.\nEducational Objectives:\n• Primary Objective: Provide high-quality education to rural youth, initially targeting the top \n1% of students from rural X class (tenth grade).\n• Course Structure:\n◦ RGUKT admits 1,000 students annually into the PUC (Pre-University Course) as \npart of a six-year integrated program culminating in a B.Tech. degree.\n◦ The focus is on providing modern educational techniques that integrate cognitive \nscience tools, such as "Learning by Example," "Learning by Doing," "Problem-\nBased Learning," and "Self-Paced Learning."\nKey Features of RGUKT, Basar:\n• Laptop Distribution: Every student is provided with a personal laptop, ensuring \nuninterrupted access to learning resources.\n• Core Values:\n◦ Integrity\n◦ Respect for all\n◦ Care for the environment\n• Emerging Fields:\n◦ RGUKT focuses on advancing knowledge in emerging ﬁelds such as Information \nTechnology, Nanotechnology, Cloud Computing, Data Analytics, and the Internet of \nThings (IoT).\n• Broad-Based Education:\n◦ Offers integrated courses in Humanities, Social Sciences, and other interdisciplinary \nareas, with an emphasis on soft skills.\nVision:\n• Mission: The university\'s vision is to provide world-class engineering education to rural \nyouth, particularly those deprived of opportunities to attend renowned institutions. The'), Document(id='60d70ca4-f2e0-4381-88fa-5a3199e5fdd1', metadata={'creationdate': "D:20241229171605Z00'00'", 'creator': 'Pages', 'moddate': "D:20241229171605Z00'00'", 'page': 0, 'page_label': '1', 'producer': 'macOS Version 15.1 (Build 24B83) Quartz PDFContext', 'source': '../rguktBasarDataset/about_rgukt/campusLife.pdf', 'title': 'campusLife', 'total_pages': 4}, page_content='Rajiv Gandhi University of Knowledge Technologies (RGUKT) Basar\nOverview:\n• Establishment: RGUKT Basar was established by the Government of Andhra Pradesh \n(A.P) in 2008 as a full-ﬂedged university.\n• Objective: The university was created to provide high-quality educational opportunities to \ntalented rural youth, primarily from Telangana and Andhra Pradesh.\n• Background:\n◦ The ﬁrst batch of 6,000 students was admitted to a six-year integrated program in \nAugust 2008.\n◦ Following the bifurcation of Andhra Pradesh in 2015, the campuses were divided \nbetween Telangana and Andhra Pradesh.\n◦ Currently, the Basar campus is the only one operational in Telangana.\nEducational Objectives:\n• Primary Objective: Provide high-quality education to rural youth, initially targeting the top \n1% of students from rural X class (tenth grade).\n• Course Structure:\n◦ RGUKT admits 1,000 students annually into the PUC (Pre-University Course) as \npart of a six-year integrated program culminating in a B.Tech. degree.\n◦ The focus is on providing modern educational techniques that integrate cognitive \nscience tools, such as "Learning by Example," "Learning by Doing," "Problem-\nBased Learning," and "Self-Paced Learning."\nKey Features of RGUKT, Basar:\n• Laptop Distribution: Every student is provided with a personal laptop, ensuring \nuninterrupted access to learning resources.\n• Core Values:\n◦ Integrity\n◦ Respect for all\n◦ Care for the environment\n• Emerging Fields:\n◦ RGUKT focuses on advancing knowledge in emerging ﬁelds such as Information \nTechnology, Nanotechnology, Cloud Computing, Data Analytics, and the Internet of \nThings (IoT).\n• Broad-Based Education:\n◦ Offers integrated courses in Humanities, Social Sciences, and other interdisciplinary \nareas, with an emphasis on soft skills.\nVision:\n• Mission: The university\'s vision is to provide world-class engineering education to rural \nyouth, particularly those deprived of opportunities to attend renowned institutions. The')], 'answer': 'I\'d be happy to provide you with the details of Rajiv Gandhi University of Knowledge Technologies (RGUKT) Basar. Here\'s some information:\n\n**Establishment:** RGUKT Basar was established by the Government of Andhra Pradesh (A.P) in 2008 as a full-pledged university.\n\n**Objective:** The university was created to provide high-quality educational opportunities to talented rural youth, primarily from Telangana and Andhra Pradesh.\n\n**Background:**\n\n* The first batch of 6,000 students was admitted to a six-year integrated program in August 2008.\n* Following the bifurcation of Andhra Pradesh in 2015, the campuses were divided between Telangana and Andhra Pradesh.\n* Currently, the Basar campus is the only one operational in Telangana.\n\n**Educational Objectives:**\n\n* Primary Objective: Provide high-quality education to rural youth, initially targeting the top 1% of students from rural X class (tenth grade).\n* Course Structure: RGUKT admits 1,000 students annually into the PUC (Pre-University Course) as part of a six-year integrated program culminating in a B.Tech. degree.\n* Focus: Providing modern educational techniques that integrate cognitive science tools, such as "Learning by Example," "Learning by Doing," "Problem-Based Learning," and "Self-Paced Learning."\n\n**Key Features:**\n\n* Laptop Distribution: Every student is provided with a personal laptop, ensuring uninterrupted access to learning resources.\n* Core Values: Integrity, Respect for all, Care for the environment.\n* Emerging Fields: RGUKT focuses on advancing knowledge in emerging fields such as Information Technology, Nanotechnology, Cloud Computing, Data Analytics, and the Internet of Things (IoT).\n* Broad-Based Education: Offers integrated courses in Humanities, Social Sciences, and other interdisciplinary areas, with an emphasis on soft skills.\n\n**Vision:** The university\'s vision is to provide world-class engineering education to rural youth, particularly those deprived of opportunities to attend renowned institutions.\n\nI hope this information is helpful, Srinu! If you have any further questions, please don\'t hesitate to ask.'}
