2025-03-12 07:18:43,999 - INFO - chat_app.services.impl.chat_service_impl - chat_service_impl.generate_response:59 - Response answer from the agent: As per the provided context, the eligibility criteria for admission to the 6-Year Integrated B.Tech Program at RGUKT Basar are as follows:

Admission to the 1st year of the 6-Year Integrated B.Tech Program will be based on merit in the Grade Point Average (GPA) and Grade obtained in each subject of SSC (10th class) or any other equivalent examination recognized by the state.

Additionally, for the purpose of admission, the following criteria will be considered:

1. Admissions will be based on merit in the Grade Point Average (GPA) and Grade obtained in each subject of SSC (10th class) or any other equivalent examination recognized by the state.
2. A deprivation score of 0.4 prescribed by the state Government under Statute 13 (3) shall be added to the 10th class GPA of those applicants who studied in non-residential Government Schools including the Zillaparishad and Municipal Schools, with an objective of providing weightage to the socio-economically challenged students in the admission process.
3. At RGUKT-Basar, admissions to 85% of the total available seats shall be reserved for the Local Candidates (Telangana State) and the remaining 15% of the seats shall be un-reserved (these seats will be filled with students from both States of Telangana and Andhra Pradesh based on merit) as specified in the Presidential Order 371 Article D in consonance to Section 95 of the A.P. Reorganization Act, 2014.

Please note that the eligibility criteria may be subject to change, and it is always best to check with the college or university for the most up-to-date information.
