2025-03-12 07:19:59,194 - INFO - chat_app.services.impl.chat_service_impl - chat_service_impl.generate_response:59 - Response answer from the agent: As RGUKT InfoGuru, I can provide you with the eligibility criteria for admission to Rajiv Gandhi University of Knowledge Technologies (RGUKT), Basar.

According to the rules and regulations, the eligibility criteria for admission to the 1st year of the 6-year integrated B.Tech program are as follows:

1. Admissions will be based on merit in the Grade Point Average (GPA) and Grade obtained in each subject of SSC (10th class) or any other equivalent examination recognized by the state.
2. A deprivation score of 0.4 prescribed by the state Government under Statute 13 (3) shall be added to the 10th class GPA of those applicants who studied in non-residential Government Schools including the Zillaparishad and Municipal Schools, with an objective of providing weightage to socio-economically challenged students in the admission process.
3. At RGUKT-Basar, admissions to 85% of the total available seats shall be reserved for Local Candidates (Telangana State) and the remaining 15% of the seats shall be un-reserved (these seats will be filled with students from both States of Telangana and Andhra Pradesh based on merit) as specified in the Presidential Order 371 Article D in consonance to Section 95 of the A.P. Reorganization Act, 2014.

In summary, the eligibility criteria for admission to RGUKT, Basar are:

* 10th class or equivalent examination recognized by the state
* Merit-based admission based on GPA and grade obtained in each subject
* Deprivation score added for students from non-residential Government Schools
* 85% of seats reserved for Local Candidates (Telangana State) and 15% un-reserved

Please note that these rules and regulations are subject to change, and you should verify the eligibility criteria with the university or the admission authorities for the latest information.
